{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Lo, how a [Bb]rose [F]e'er [C]blooming [Bb]From [F]tender [Dm]stem [C]hath [F]sprung,
[F]Of Jesse's [Bb]lineage [C]coming [Bb]As [F]men [C/E]of [Dm]old [C7]have [F]sung.
[F]It came, [Gm]afloweret [C]bright,
[C]Amid the [F]cold [Bb]of [F]winter [Dm]When [Gm]half [Am]spent [Gm/Bb]was [F/C]the [C]night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Isaiah [Bb]'twas [C]foretold it,
[F]The Rose I [Dm]have [F]in [Dm]mind,
[F]With Mary [C]we [Bb]beheld [C7]it,
[F]The [Gm]virgin [F]mother [C]kind.
[F]To [Gm]show [Am]God's [F]love [Gm]aright
[F]She bore [Gm]to [Am]them [F]a [Gm]Savior,
[C]When [F]half spent [Dm]was [Am]the [F/C]night.
{end_of_verse}
